 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 533807,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Do regular heptagons tessellate the plane by themselves?<br>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/ef6ea0465427fe7c.png\" alt=\"A tessellation pattern is made up of six heptagons.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>For regular polygons to be able to tesselate, the shapes must meet at a vertex so that the interior angles have a sum of 360°.</p>\n<p>A heptagon has seven sides, so <span data-math=\"n = 7\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The measure of each interior angle of a regular polygon with <i>n</i> sides is given by <span data-math=\"a = \\frac{{\\left( {n - 2} \\right)180^\\circ }}{n}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"a = \\frac{{\\left( {n - 2} \\right)180^\\circ }}{n} = \\frac{{\\left( {7 - 2} \\right)180^\\circ }}{7} = \\frac{{\\left( 5 \\right)180^\\circ }}{7} = \\frac{{900}}{7} \\approx 127.57^\\circ \"></span></p>\n<p>Since the interior angles of a heptagon are not integer factors of 360°, it is impossible to tesselate with heptagons by themselves.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "No"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
